```python
def bubble_sort(nums):
    result = list(nums)
    n = len(result)
    for i in range(n - 1):
        swapped = False
        for j in range(n - i - 1):
            if result[j] > result[j + 1]:
                result[j], result[j + 1] = result[j + 1], result[j]
                swapped = True
        if not swapped:
            break
    return result
```

This implementation fixes the original function by adding a flag `swapped` to track if any swaps were made in the inner loop. If no swaps were made, it means the list is already sorted and the algorithm can terminate early. This reduces the time complexity of the algorithm from O(n^2) to O(n) in the best case.
